+PagerDuty & Incident Playbook (Aegis)
+
+Overview
+- This playbook describes how Aegis forwards critical HIL/formal failures to PagerDuty and SIEM and how remediation tickets are created.
+
+Flow
+1. HIL workflow completes and writes a summary.json with results.  
+2. CI watcher (.github/workflows/hil_failure_alert_and_remediate.yml) reads summary.json and, on failures, posts an alert to ops/incident/pagerduty_forwarder.py.  
+3. PagerDuty event triggers on-call rotation; SIEM stores full details and the remediation automation opens a GitHub issue via ops/incident/auto_remediate_and_ticket.py.  
+
+Playbook steps for on-call
+- Acknowledge the incident in PagerDuty.  
+- Inspect /tmp/hil_closure/summary.json and captured artifacts (logs, waveforms, traces).  
+- If fix is immediate, push a hotfix branch and re-run PoA for the target. If fix requires hardware, schedule an HIL re-run window.  
+- Close the GitHub issue with remediation notes and evidence references.
